n to be  present for the national service of  remembrance  so that very important service at the  cenotaph which is a focal point a real  moment for the royal family during any  year they're saying that she does still  intend to be there present of course we  know in recent years she has handed over  the responsibility of laying that wreath  on behalf of the nation at the foot of  the cenotaph that responsibility is now  carried out  by the prince of wales but still for the  last few years the queen has been there  on the balcon balcony watching as her  son and heir has carried out that duty  on her behalf also the palace i  understand from them that the queen is  in good spirits of course that has  become  a stock phrase that we've heard them  saying quite a lot also we understand  that she recorded her cop 26 speech this  afternoon of course you have to remember  that it was only on tuesday that we  found out that the queen was no longer  going to be attending that really  important uh reception that she was due  to host at the opening of cop26 she was  due to welcome those world leaders  instead it's now going to be the  responsibility of the prince of wales  the duchess of cornwall and the duke and  duchess of cambridge um also i think for  the palace what they really want to  stress is that light duties are  continuing so yesterday for example we  saw the queen  carrying out a virtual engagement where  she handed over  virtually  a the queen's medal for poetry she was  at windsor castle the recipient was at  buckingham palace um but i think the  overriding message also is that really  the doctors are just trying to be  sensible they're taking every precaution  to make sure that the 95 year old  monarch gets better of course we don't  know what's wrong with her we haven't  been given those details all we know is  that last week she did spend a night in  hospital she did have preliminary tests  what for we don't know  hey rhiannon thank you
 

